  ($q$cs-214$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Cross-Text Connections$q$, 2, $q$Text 1: Veterinarian A recommends commercially formulated pet food, arguing that it is nutritionally balanced according to standards tested across large populations of animals.

Text 2: Veterinarian B recommends raw diets tailored to an individual pet, arguing that commercial formulas use a one-size-fits-all approach that cannot account for a specific animal's needs.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes a key difference between the two veterinarians' recommendations?$q$, $q$["Veterinarian A favors standardized, tested nutrition, while Veterinarian B favors individualized diets.","Both veterinarians agree that raw diets are nutritionally balanced for all pets.","Veterinarian B recommends commercial pet food over raw diets.","Veterinarian A argues that pets' needs vary too much for any standard diet."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Veterinarian A values standardized, population-tested nutrition, while Veterinarian B values diets tailored to the individual animal — the contrast in the correct answer.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-215$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Cross-Text Connections$q$, 2, $q$Text 1: Meteorologist A argues that rapid hurricane intensification is driven primarily by unusually warm ocean surface temperatures that fuel storm energy.

Text 2: Meteorologist B argues that low atmospheric wind shear is the more decisive factor, noting storms over similarly warm waters that failed to intensify rapidly when wind shear remained high.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes a key difference between the two meteorologists' explanations?$q$, $q$["Meteorologist A emphasizes ocean temperature, while Meteorologist B emphasizes atmospheric wind shear.","Both meteorologists agree that wind shear is irrelevant to intensification.","Meteorologist B relies exclusively on ocean temperature data.","Meteorologist A argues that wind shear is the decisive factor."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Meteorologist A points to warm ocean temperatures, while Meteorologist B points to low wind shear, citing storms over warm water that failed to intensify when shear was high — the contrast in the correct answer.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-216$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Cross-Text Connections$q$, 2, $q$Text 1: Labor economist A argues that gig work expands economic opportunity by letting workers set flexible schedules unavailable in traditional jobs.

Text 2: Labor economist B argues that this flexibility comes at the cost of job security, pointing to survey data showing gig workers report far greater income volatility month to month than traditionally employed workers.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the relationship between the two economists' claims?$q$, $q$["Economist B's data complicates Economist A's claim by weighing a cost against the flexibility it emphasizes.","Economist B's findings confirm exactly what Economist A argues.","Both economists agree that gig work provides no flexibility.","Economist A argues that gig workers have highly stable incomes."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Economist B's income-volatility data introduces a cost that complicates, rather than confirms, Economist A's purely positive framing of gig work's flexibility.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-217$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Cross-Text Connections$q$, 1, $q$Text 1: Art conservator A recommends cleaning old paintings with traditional solvents, arguing that decades of documented use make the technique's effects predictable.

Text 2: Art conservator B recommends laser cleaning, arguing that it removes grime more precisely without the risk of solvents seeping into and damaging original paint layers.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes a key difference between the two conservators' approaches?$q$, $q$["Conservator A favors a long-established method, while Conservator B favors a more precise, lower-risk technique.","Both conservators agree that solvents never damage paintings.","Conservator B recommends solvents over laser cleaning.","Conservator A argues that laser cleaning is more precise."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Conservator A values the predictability of a long-used solvent method, while Conservator B values the precision and lower risk of laser cleaning — the contrast in the correct answer.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-218$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Cross-Text Connections$q$, 2, $q$Text 1: Immunologist A argues that booster shots should be given at fixed yearly intervals to maintain consistent population-wide immunity.

