  ($q$cs-220$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Cross-Text Connections$q$, 1, $q$Text 1: Agricultural scientist A argues that vertical farms will soon outcompete traditional farms for leafy greens, citing their drastically lower water use and year-round growing seasons.

Text 2: Agricultural scientist B argues that vertical farms remain far more expensive per crop due to high energy costs for artificial lighting, limiting them to premium markets for now.$q$, $q$Based on the texts, how would Agricultural scientist B most likely respond to Agricultural scientist A's claim?$q$, $q$["By pointing to high energy costs as a barrier that limits vertical farming's near-term competitiveness","By agreeing that vertical farms will soon replace traditional farms entirely","By arguing that vertical farms use more water than traditional farms","By claiming that lighting costs do not affect vertical farming's expenses"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Agricultural scientist B's position is that high energy costs limit vertical farms 'to premium markets for now,' directly countering A's claim that they will soon outcompete traditional farms.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-221$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Cross-Text Connections$q$, 2, $q$Text 1: Musicologist A argues that a folk music genre's distinctive rhythm spread through oral tradition passed between traveling musicians at regional festivals.

