An art historian responds that the criterion of depiction is itself a convention, one that photography made obsolete as a measure of painterly value.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the historian's response to the critic?$q$, $q$["It challenges the standard the critic uses to judge art.","It offers a biography of the critic.","It agrees that abstraction is a lesser form.","It restates the critic's claim in new words."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The historian questions the criterion (depiction) that grounds the critic's evaluation.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-459$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Cross-Text Connections$q$, 2, $q$Text 1
