Text 2
Climatologist Tom Weber says that while day-specific forecasts beyond ten days are unreliable, seasonal outlooks that predict whether a period will be warmer or wetter than average can be useful.$q$, $q$Based on the texts, how would Weber most likely view Nair's claim?$q$, $q$["As completely correct","As too broad, since some long-range predictions have value","As irrelevant to forecasting","As understating the reliability of day-specific forecasts"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Weber agrees about day-specific forecasts but notes seasonal outlooks are useful.$q$, null),
