  ($q$ei-496$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Expression of Ideas$q$, $q$Rhetorical Synthesis$q$, 2, $q$A student has gathered the following notes:
• The Eiffel Tower was completed in 1889.
• It was built as the entrance arch for the World's Fair in Paris.
• It was originally intended to stand for only twenty years.$q$, $q$The student wants to explain why the tower was built and how long it was meant to stand. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?$q$, $q$["Built as the entrance arch for the Paris World's Fair, the Eiffel Tower was meant to stand for only twenty years.","The Eiffel Tower was completed in 1889.","Though completed in 1889, the Eiffel Tower was originally intended to stand for only twenty years.","Completed in 1889, the Eiffel Tower served as the entrance arch for the World's Fair in Paris."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The goal calls for two specific pieces of information from the notes. This choice is the only one that includes both of them; each of the other choices omits one of them or relies on a note that is not relevant to the goal.$q$, null),
  ($q$ei-497$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Expression of Ideas$q$, $q$Transitions$q$, 1, $q$Some animals use tools in remarkably sophisticated ways. ______ crows bend wire into hooks to retrieve food.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?$q$, $q$["In contrast,","As a result,","For instance,","Additionally,"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$The second sentence expresses a specific example relative to the first sentence, so "For instance" is the logical transition. The other choices signal relationships the sentences do not have.$q$, null),
  ($q$ei-498$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Expression of Ideas$q$, $q$Transitions$q$, 1, $q$Tidal energy is highly predictable. ______ it produces no greenhouse gases during operation.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?$q$, $q$["Therefore,","For example,","Afterward,","Furthermore,"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$The second sentence expresses an additional, supporting point relative to the first sentence, so "Furthermore" is the logical transition. The other choices signal relationships the sentences do not have.$q$, null),
  ($q$ei-499$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Expression of Ideas$q$, $q$Rhetorical Synthesis$q$, 2, $q$A student has gathered the following notes:
