  ($q$conv-478$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Standard English Conventions$q$, $q$Boundaries$q$, 2, $q$The museum's ancient scrolls are extremely fragile______curators display only reproductions.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?$q$, $q$[", ","; ","; and "," "]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Both "The museum's ancient scrolls are extremely fragile" and "curators display only reproductions" are independent clauses. They can be joined with a semicolon; a comma alone creates a comma splice and no punctuation creates a run-on sentence, and a semicolon should not be combined with "and."$q$, null),
  ($q$conv-479$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Standard English Conventions$q$, $q$Boundaries$q$, 1, $q$Rainfall in the valley has doubled since 1990______and farmers have switched to new crops.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?$q$, $q$[", ","; ",": "," "]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$A coordinating conjunction ("and") joining two independent clauses must be preceded by a comma.$q$, null),
  ($q$conv-480$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Standard English Conventions$q$, $q$Boundaries$q$, 2, $q$Rainfall in the valley has doubled since 1990______farmers have switched to new crops.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?$q$, $q$["; ","; and ",", "," "]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Both "Rainfall in the valley has doubled since 1990" and "farmers have switched to new crops" are independent clauses. They can be joined with a semicolon; a comma alone creates a comma splice and no punctuation creates a run-on sentence, and a semicolon should not be combined with "and."$q$, null),
  ($q$conv-481$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Standard English Conventions$q$, $q$Form, Structure, and Sense$q$, 2, $q$When the storm hit the coast last September, residents ______ to higher ground before the flooding began.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?$q$, $q$["already move","had already moved","have already moved","will already move"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$The past perfect "had already moved" shows an action completed before another past event (the flooding began).$q$, null),
  ($q$conv-482$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Standard English Conventions$q$, $q$Boundaries$q$, 1, $q$Maya practiced the violin every morning before school______so her audition piece was nearly flawless.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?$q$, $q$[" ",", ",": ","; "]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$A coordinating conjunction ("so") joining two independent clauses must be preceded by a comma.$q$, null),
