  ($q$alg-687$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear functions$q$, 2, null, $q$<table class="data-table"><tr><th>x</th><th>f(x)</th></tr><tr><td>−3</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>0</td><td>−8</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>−11</td></tr></table>The table shows three values of x and their corresponding values of f(x), where f is a linear function. Which equation defines f?$q$, $q$["f(x) = −3x + 8","f(x) = 3x − 8","f(x) = −8x − 3","f(x) = −3x − 8"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$The slope is (−8 − 1)/(0 − (−3)) = −3. Using x = −3: 1 = −3(−3) + b gives b = −8. So f(x) = −3x − 8.$q$, null),
