  ($q$pd-507$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$q$, $q$Evaluating statistical claims$q$, 2, null, $q$A survey of 1,000 randomly selected shoppers found that those who bought organic produce also tended to exercise more. Which conclusion is best supported?$q$, $q$["There is an association between buying organic produce and exercising more among shoppers like those surveyed.","Buying organic produce causes people to exercise more.","Exercising causes people to buy organic produce.","Shoppers who do not buy organic produce never exercise."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The data were observational, so they show an association but not a cause-and-effect relationship.$q$, null),
  ($q$pd-508$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$q$, $q$Two-variable data$q$, 2, null, $q$A line of best fit for a data set relating the number of hours a plant receives sunlight (h) to its height in centimeters (H) is H = 22 + 4h. According to this model, what is the predicted height in centimeters when h = 7?$q$, $q$["95","50","158","33"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Substitute h = 7: 22 + 4(7) = 50.$q$, null),
  ($q$pd-509$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$q$, $q$One-variable data$q$, 2, null, $q$The mean score of 5 students on a quiz is 85. A new student scores 103, and the score is added to the data. What is the mean score of all 6 students?$q$, $q$["88","89","85","94"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The original total is 5 × 85 = 425. Adding 103 gives 528. Dividing by 6 gives 88.$q$, null),
