  ($q$pd-514$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$q$, $q$Ratios and proportions$q$, 1, null, $q$The ratio of cats to dogs among the animals at a shelter is 3 to 4. If there are 21 in total, how many are dogs?$q$, $q$["10.5","4","12","9"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$The 7 parts account for 21, so each part is 21/7 = 3. The dogs make up 4 parts: 12.$q$, null),
  ($q$pd-515$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$q$, $q$Percentages$q$, 1, null, $q$A pair of headphones is on sale for $105, which is 30% off the original price. What was the original price, in dollars?$q$, $q$["150","135","136.5","350"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The sale price is 70% of the original, so 0.7x = 105. Then x = 105/0.7 = 150.$q$, null),
