  ($q$pd-524$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$q$, $q$Probability$q$, 1, null, $q$A jar contains 12 red candies, 8 green candies, and 7 blue candies. If one candy is chosen at random, what is the probability that it is NOT red?$q$, $q$["8/27","4/9","5/4","5/9"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$There are 27 candies, and 15 of them are not red. The probability is 15/27 = 5/9.$q$, null),
