  ($q$pd-548$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$q$, $q$Ratios and proportions$q$, 1, null, $q$The ratio of red marbles to blue marbles in a bag is 8:9. If the bag contains 136 marbles in total, how many are red?$q$, $q$["64","72","17","128"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$There are 17 parts in total, so each part is 136/17 = 8 marbles. Red: 8 × 8 = 64.$q$, null),
  ($q$pd-549$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$q$, $q$Evaluating statistical claims$q$, 2, null, $q$In a study, patients with mild headaches were randomly assigned to either receive a new pain reliever or not receive it. The group that received a new pain reliever showed a statistically significant improvement in reported pain. Which conclusion is best supported by the study?$q$, $q$["A new pain reliever improves reported pain for everyone, regardless of group.","Neither group's reported pain changed.","A new pain reliever likely caused the improvement in reported pain for patients with mild headaches like those in the study.","Reported pain and a new pain reliever are correlated, but no causal conclusion is possible."]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$Random assignment supports a causal conclusion, but only for populations similar to the participants.$q$, null),
  ($q$pd-550$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$q$, $q$Two-variable data$q$, 2, null, $q$A line of best fit for a scatterplot is y = 0.5x + 71, where x is the number of hours of practice and y is the performance score. Which of the following is the best interpretation of the number 0.5 in this context?$q$, $q$["The performance score increases by 0.5 percent each time.","The number of hours of practice is predicted to be 0.5 when the performance score is 71.","When the number of hours of practice is 0, the predicted performance score is 0.5.","For each 1-unit increase in the number of hours of practice, the predicted performance score increases by 0.5."]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$The slope is the predicted change in y for each 1-unit increase in x.$q$, null),
