  ($q$pd-722$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$q$, $q$Inference from sample statistics$q$, 2, null, $q$A random sample of 80 residents of a town was surveyed, and 28 of them said they use the public library at least once a month. The town has 2,000 residents in all. Based on the sample, which is the best estimate of the total number of residents who would say this?$q$, $q$["280","700","560","1,300"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$The sample proportion is 28/80. Applying it to all 2,000 residents: 2,000 × 28/80 = 700.$q$, null),
  ($q$pd-723$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$q$, $q$Inference from sample statistics$q$, 2, null, $q$A random sample of 100 households of a county was surveyed, and 47 of them said they compost food scraps. The county has 1,200 households in all. Based on the sample, which is the best estimate of the total number of households who would say this?$q$, $q$["564","664","636","470"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The sample proportion is 47/100. Applying it to all 1,200 households: 1,200 × 47/100 = 564.$q$, null),
