  ($q$pd-729$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$q$, $q$Two-variable data$q$, 2, null, $q$The line of best fit for a data set is y = 0.35x + 120, where x is the number of years since 2010 and y is the average price, in dollars, of a movie ticket. Which is the best interpretation of 0.35 in this context?$q$, $q$["The predicted value of y when x = 0.35","A predicted increase of $0.35 in the ticket price every 0.35 years","The predicted ticket price in 2010","A predicted increase of $0.35 in the average ticket price each year"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$The slope 0.35 is the predicted change in y for each increase of 1 in x, so it represents a predicted increase of $0.35 in the average ticket price each year.$q$, null),
