  ($q$geo-459$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Special right triangles$q$, 2, null, $q$In a 30°-60°-90° triangle, the shortest side has a length of 11. What is the length of the longest leg?$q$, $q$["11√2","22","121","11√3"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$In a 30-60-90 triangle the sides are x, x√3, and 2x. The shorter leg is 11, so the longer leg is 11√3.$q$, null),
  ($q$geo-460$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Circles$q$, 2, null, $q$A circle has a radius of 24 centimeters. An arc of the circle is intercepted by a central angle of 240°. What is the length of the arc, in centimeters?$q$, $q$["32π","48π","384π","64π"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Arc length = (θ/360)·2πr = (240/360)(2π)(24) = 32π.$q$, null),
  ($q$geo-461$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Right triangle trigonometry$q$, 1, null, $q$For an acute angle, sin(59°) = cos(x°). What is the value of x?$q$, $q$["59","149","121","31"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$The sine of an angle equals the cosine of its complement, so x = 90 − 59 = 31.$q$, null),
  ($q$geo-462$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Coordinate geometry$q$, 2, null, $q$The midpoint of segment AB is (−6, 7). Point A has coordinates (5, 1). What are the coordinates of point B?$q$, $q$["(−17, 13)","(−11, 6)","(−12, 14)","(−1, 8)"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Midpoint x: (5 + x)/2 = −6 → x = −17. Midpoint y: (1 + y)/2 = 7 → y = 13.$q$, null),
  ($q$geo-463$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Similar triangles$q$, 2, null, $q$At the same time of day, a 5-foot post casts a 9-foot shadow, and a nearby tree casts a 27-foot shadow. Assuming the post and tree are both vertical, what is the height of the tree, in feet?$q$, $q$["15","32","243/5","23"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The similar triangles give h/27 = 5/9, so the tree is 27·5/9 = 15 feet tall.$q$, null),
  ($q$geo-464$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Right triangle trigonometry$q$, 1, null, $q$In right triangle ABC, angle B is the right angle, AB = 21, BC = 20, and AC = 29. What is the value of tan A?$q$, $q$["21/20","21/29","20/21","20/29"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$Relative to angle A: opposite = BC = 20, adjacent = AB = 21, hypotenuse = 29. tan A = opp/adj = 20/21.$q$, null),
  ($q$geo-465$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Special right triangles$q$, 1, null, $q$A square has a side length of 6. What is the length of its diagonal?$q$, $q$["12","6√3","36","6√2"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$The diagonal splits the square into two 45-45-90 triangles, so the diagonal is 6√2.$q$, null),
