  ($q$geo-467$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Triangle angles$q$, 2, null, $q$The angles of a triangle measure (3x + 3)°, (4x + 6)°, and (2x + 18)°. What is the measure, in degrees, of the largest angle?$q$, $q$["54","52","17","74"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$The angles sum to 180: 9x + 27 = 180 → x = 17. The angles are 54°, 74°, and 52°, so the largest is 74°.$q$, null),
  ($q$geo-468$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Circles$q$, 2, null, $q$The circumference of a circle is 6π centimeters. What is the area of the circle, in square centimeters?$q$, $q$["18π","9π","6π","36π"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$C = 2πr = 6π gives r = 3, so A = πr² = 9π.$q$, null),
  ($q$geo-469$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Circles$q$, 1, null, $q$In the xy-plane, a circle is given by the equation (x + 6)² + (y − 3)² = 9. What is the radius of the circle?$q$, $q$["−3","6","3","9"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$The standard form is (x − h)² + (y − k)² = r². Since r² = 9, r = 3.$q$, null),
