  ($q$geo-472$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Triangle angles$q$, 1, null, $q$The measures of the angles of a triangle are in the ratio 1 : 3 : 5. What is the measure, in degrees, of the largest angle?$q$, $q$["90","20","80","100"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$The ratio parts total 9, so each part is 180/9 = 20°. The largest angle is 5·20 = 100°.$q$, null),
  ($q$geo-473$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Triangle angles$q$, 1, null, $q$The measures of the angles of a triangle are in the ratio 1 : 2 : 3. What is the measure, in degrees, of the largest angle?$q$, $q$["177","60","30","90"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$The ratio parts total 6, so each part is 180/6 = 30°. The largest angle is 3·30 = 90°.$q$, null),
  ($q$geo-474$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Right triangle trigonometry$q$, 2, null, $q$In right triangle ABC, angle B is the right angle and sin A = 20/29. If AB = 63, what is the length of BC?$q$, $q$["87","43","63","60"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$sin A = BC/AC = 20/29, so the legs and hypotenuse form a 20-21-29 triangle scaled by k. AB = 21k = 63 gives k = 3, so BC = 20k = 60.$q$, null),
  ($q$geo-475$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Coordinate geometry$q$, 1, null, $q$In the xy-plane, what is the distance between the points (−4, 2) and (4, 17)?$q$, $q$["23","18","7","17"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$Distance = √(8² + 15²) = √289 = 17.$q$, null),
  ($q$geo-476$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Special right triangles$q$, 2, null, $q$A right triangle has two equal angles and a leg of length 6. What is the length of its hypotenuse?$q$, $q$["6","6√2","6√3","12"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$The triangle is a 45°-45°-90° triangle, so the hypotenuse is the leg times √2: 6√2.$q$, null),
  ($q$geo-477$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Similar triangles$q$, 2, null, $q$Triangle ABC is similar to triangle DEF, where AB corresponds to DE and BC corresponds to EF. AB = 6, BC = 9, and DE = 12. What is the length of EF?$q$, $q$["15","11","18","24"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$The scale factor from ABC to DEF is 12/6 = 2. So EF = 2 × 9 = 18.$q$, null),
  ($q$geo-478$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Lines and angles$q$, 2, null, $q$Two angles form a linear pair. One angle measures x° and the other measures (3x + 12)°. What is the value of x?$q$, $q$["52","45","42","56"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$The angles of a linear pair are supplementary: x + (3x + 12) = 180. So 4x = 168 and x = 42.$q$, null),
  ($q$geo-479$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Right triangle trigonometry$q$, 2, null, $q$In right triangle ABC, the right angle is at C, AB = 5, BC = 3, and AC = 4. What is the value of cos B?$q$, $q$["4/5","3/4","4/3","3/5"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$For angle B, the opposite side is 4, the adjacent side is 3, and the hypotenuse is 5. cos = adjacent/hypotenuse = 3/5.$q$, null),
  ($q$geo-480$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Special right triangles$q$, 2, null, $q$The hypotenuse of a right triangle with two congruent sides is 4√2. What is the area of the triangle?$q$, $q$["4","32","8","16"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$The legs of a 45°-45°-90° triangle are hypotenuse/√2 = 4. Area = ½ × 4 × 4 = 8.$q$, null),
