  ($q$geo-714$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Circles$q$, 2, null, $q$The equation x² − 8x + y² − 14y = −16 defines a circle in the xy-plane. What is the radius of the circle?$q$, $q$["7","4","11","49"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Complete the square: (x − 4)² − 16 + (y − 7)² − 49 = −16. So (x − 4)² + (y − 7)² = 49, and the radius is √49 = 7.$q$, null),
