  ($q$geo-718$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Triangle angles$q$, 2, null, $q$In triangle PQR, the measures of angles P and Q are 22° and 67°. An exterior angle at vertex R measures (3x + 5)°. What is the value of x?$q$, $q$["89","26","31","28"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$An exterior angle equals the sum of the two remote interior angles: 3x + 5 = 22 + 67 = 89. So 3x = 84 and x = 28.$q$, null),
  ($q$geo-719$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Right triangle trigonometry$q$, 2, null, $q$In a right triangle, one acute angle measures x°. If cos(x°) = 0.12, what is the value of sin((90 − x)°)?$q$, $q$["8.33","0.88","0.12","−0.12"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$The two acute angles of a right triangle are complementary, and cos(x°) = sin((90 − x)°). So sin((90 − x)°) = 0.12.$q$, null),
