  ($q$geo-721$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Triangle angles$q$, 2, null, $q$In triangle PQR, the measures of angles P and Q are 62° and 79°. An exterior angle at vertex R measures (2x − 5)°. What is the value of x?$q$, $q$["68","141","73","22"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$An exterior angle equals the sum of the two remote interior angles: 2x − 5 = 62 + 79 = 141. So 2x = 146 and x = 73.$q$, null),
