  ($q$adv-bb11$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Nonlinear functions$q$, 2, null, $q$The function f(x) = (x − 6)<sup>2</sup> + 5 gives a toy rocket's height above the ground, f(x), in inches, x seconds after it started moving, where 0 ≤ x ≤ 12. Which of the following is the best interpretation of the vertex of the graph of y = f(x) in the xy-plane?$q$, $q$["The toy rocket's height was 6 inches when it started moving.","The toy rocket's minimum height was 5 inches.","The toy rocket's minimum height was 6 inches.","The toy rocket's height was 5 inches when it started moving."]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$In vertex form f(x) = a(x − h)<sup>2</sup> + k, the vertex is (h, k). Here the vertex is (6, 5). Since a > 0, the parabola opens upward, so 5 is the minimum value of f, reached when x = 6. The height when it started moving is f(0) = 41, not a coordinate of the vertex.$q$, null),
