  ($q$adv-bb31$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponential functions$q$, 3, null, $q$f(x) = 2,000(0.72)<sup>x/12</sup><br><br>The function f gives the value, in dollars, of a certain piece of equipment after x months. If the value of the equipment decreases each year by p% of its value the preceding year, what is the value of p?$q$, $q$["336","72","28","2.33"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$Since x is in months, x/12 is the number of years, so the value is multiplied by 0.72 once per year. A yearly multiplier of 0.72 means the value keeps 72% of the preceding year's value, a decrease of 28% each year. So p = 28.$q$, null),
