  ($q$pd-bb11$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$q$, $q$Inference from sample statistics$q$, 2, null, $q$To estimate the proportion of a population that has a certain characteristic, a random sample was selected from the population. Based on the sample, it is estimated that the proportion of the population that has the characteristic is 0.74, with an associated margin of error of 0.05. Based on this estimate and margin of error, which of the following is the most appropriate conclusion about the proportion of the population that has the characteristic?$q$, $q$["It is plausible that the proportion is between 0.69 and 0.79.","The proportion is exactly 0.74.","It is plausible that the proportion is less than 0.69.","It is plausible that the proportion is greater than 0.79."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The margin of error gives a range of plausible values around the estimate: 0.74 − 0.05 = 0.69 to 0.74 + 0.05 = 0.79. Values outside that range are not supported by the data, and a sample can't show that the proportion is exactly 0.74.$q$, null),
