  ($q$pd-bb40$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$q$, $q$One-variable data$q$, 3, null, $q$Data set A consists of the 15 values 10, 11, 18, 21, 24, 25, 28, 30, 31, 34, 34, 35, 35, 39, 40. Data set B is created by multiplying each value in data set A by 3. Which of the following correctly compares the medians and the ranges of data sets A and B?$q$, $q$["The median of data set B is greater than the median of data set A, and the range of data set B is greater than the range of data set A.","The median of data set B is greater than the median of data set A, and the range of data set B is equal to the range of data set A.","The median of data set B is equal to the median of data set A, and the range of data set B is less than the range of data set A.","The median of data set B is less than the median of data set A, and the range of data set B is greater than the range of data set A."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Multiplying every value by 3 multiplies the median by 3; since the values are positive, the median increases. The range is also multiplied by 3, so it increases too.$q$, null),
  ($q$geo-bb1$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Circles$q$, 2, null, $q$The equation (x − 5)<sup>2</sup> + (y + 6)<sup>2</sup> = 81 represents circle A. Circle B is obtained by shifting circle A down 1 unit in the xy-plane. Which of the following equations represents circle B?$q$, $q$["(x − 6)<sup>2</sup> + (y + 6)<sup>2</sup> = 81","(x − 5)<sup>2</sup> + (y + 5)<sup>2</sup> = 81","(x − 5)<sup>2</sup> + (y + 7)<sup>2</sup> = 81","(x − 4)<sup>2</sup> + (y + 6)<sup>2</sup> = 81"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$Circle A has center (5, −6) and radius 9. Shifting it down 1 unit moves the center to (5, −7) and leaves the radius unchanged, so circle B is (x − 5)<sup>2</sup> + (y + 7)<sup>2</sup> = 81. Remember that (x − h) and (y − k) use the opposite sign of the center's coordinates.$q$, null),
