  ($q$geo-bb5$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Circles$q$, 2, null, $q$The equation x<sup>2</sup> + (y − 3)<sup>2</sup> = 36 represents circle A. Circle B is obtained by shifting circle A up 4 units in the xy-plane. Which of the following equations represents circle B?$q$, $q$["x<sup>2</sup> + (y − 7)<sup>2</sup> = 36","x<sup>2</sup> + (y + 1)<sup>2</sup> = 36","(x + 4)<sup>2</sup> + (y − 3)<sup>2</sup> = 36","(x − 4)<sup>2</sup> + (y − 3)<sup>2</sup> = 36"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Circle A has center (0, 3) and radius 6. Shifting it up 4 units moves the center to (0, 7) and leaves the radius unchanged, so circle B is x<sup>2</sup> + (y − 7)<sup>2</sup> = 36. Remember that (x − h) and (y − k) use the opposite sign of the center's coordinates.$q$, null),
