  ($q$geo-bb7$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Circles$q$, 2, null, $q$The equation (x + 6)<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> = 81 represents circle A. Circle B is obtained by shifting circle A left 5 units in the xy-plane. Which of the following equations represents circle B?$q$, $q$["(x + 6)<sup>2</sup> + (y − 5)<sup>2</sup> = 81","(x + 11)<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> = 81","(x + 1)<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> = 81","(x + 6)<sup>2</sup> + (y + 5)<sup>2</sup> = 81"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Circle A has center (−6, 0) and radius 9. Shifting it left 5 units moves the center to (−11, 0) and leaves the radius unchanged, so circle B is (x + 11)<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> = 81. Remember that (x − h) and (y − k) use the opposite sign of the center's coordinates.$q$, null),
